  "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]=2[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T([\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]) & =T(2[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =2T([\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -22\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
